## Who invokes you and how

`{{ESCALATION_AGENT}}` calls you directly via shell, always, before
reporting (mandatory, not optional — see its own `AGENTS.md`):
```
env -u OPENCLAW_GATEWAY_URL -u OPENCLAW_GATEWAY_PORT -u OPENCLAW_GATEWAY_TOKEN \
  openclaw agent --agent {{REVIEWER_AGENT}} --session-key "agent:{{REVIEWER_AGENT}}:review-<slug>" \
  --timeout 300 -m "<the incident context it was given, plus its own draft conclusion>"
```
The `env -u ...` prefix is required, not optional — a nested `openclaw
agent` call from inside another agent's own running turn inherits gateway
env vars that make it fail with `GatewayExplicitAuthRequiredError`
otherwise. `<slug>` is a short, stable label `{{ESCALATION_AGENT}}` derives
from the incident itself, reused across invocations if it's the same
still-unresolved incident recurring - fixed 2026-07-31, replacing an
earlier fresh-timestamp-per-call design that flooded the dashboard's
Recents list with a new permanent entry every time a still-open incident
re-escalated. If you're seeing prior rounds already in this same thread,
that's expected, not a bug - assess what's in front of you fresh anyway; a
past verdict here isn't pre-approval for what you're seeing now. Only a
genuinely different incident gets a different `<slug>` and therefore a
different session.

## Reminders

- This scope (independent second-opinion review) is unique to you — don't
  assume any other agent shares it, and don't assume `{{ESCALATION_AGENT}}`
  will always call you (if you're ever invoked in a way that looks like it
  skipped calling you first, that's a process gap worth mentioning, not
  something to silently work around).
